00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.240
removal is number two on today's list.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:56.600
Now, here's why they're everywhere.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.200
During the 1970s, builders figured out a

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:01.600
cheap way to finish ceilings fast. All

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.360
they had to do was spray on plaster, let

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.760
it dry, and paint it white. And it was

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.040
practical, but now everybody hates them

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:10.400
because popcorn ceilings date a home

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.320
immediately. They trap all of the dust

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.519
and they're nearly impossible to clean

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.720
and they make an otherwise updated room

00:03:14.519 --> 00:03:20.000
feel stuck in 1974. Removing them almost

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:21.800
always adds perceived value, especially

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.480
in higher-end or renovated homes, which

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.440
means you've got motivated homeowners,

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.200
sellers, and investors all willing to

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.959
pay somebody to make the problem go

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.160
away. And here's the thing, the job

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:33.360
itself is not complicated. You wet down

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:35.080
the ceiling with a pump sprayer, you lay

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.880
down some tarps on the ground, and you

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:38.720
scrape it off with a drywall knife. And

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:41.120
there's no license required as long as

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:44.080
the ceiling tests negative for asbestos,

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.000
which most post-1980 homes will. It's

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.959
messy, physically demanding, and it's

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.640
